# Pipeline — Cursor baseline

The universal contract lives in `AGENTS.md`; canonical policy in
`scripts/codex_protocol_model.py`. This rule carries only the always-on
Cursor boundaries.

- Preserve unrelated work, stage explicit pathspecs, and use the worktree's
  native Git index (never set `GIT_INDEX_FILE`). No destructive Git without
  explicit user authorization.
- No formal seat exists unless this chat is the registered top-level chat of
  a reserved `cursor-seat/<seat>` worktree. Absence of a seat means no seat
  authority — it is not a special workflow to reason about.
- The project hook may deny native file edits in unbound sessions or convert
  governed mutations and remote Git effects into one in-app approval; that
  is expected behavior, not an error. Use the shell path it names, and never
  edit mailbox, lock, or `.cursor/runtime/` state directly.
- A hook approval card is the effect authority for that exact command; do
  not re-ask in chat. Remote Git effects and paid spend each surface their
  own approval. Native file-tool edits imply no effect authority.
- For seat, mailbox, review, worktree, or coordination protocol work, load
  `.cursor/rules/cursor-seats.mdc` and `docs/protocol/cursor/continuation.md`.
